      "artist": "NPS Photo",
      "description": "a man in national park service uniform sits on a bench inside a circular acrylic sculpture with marine debris encased inside. The top of the sculpture says \"Biscayne National Park\" and next to the sculpture is a wayside.\nThe marine debris display at Biscayne National Park is located in the Dante Fascell Visitor Center. The display features an acrylic sculpture with marine debris encased inside and a bench to sit in the middle of the ring - the perfect place to snap a photo and share on social media to spread awareness. The exhibit also features a bi-lingual wayside.\nKeywords: marine debris",
